Test corpus
  snapshot/testdata/rust/ vendors Rust naga's WGSL and GLSL test inputs, test
  parameters and reference outputs verbatim, with their LICENSE.MIT and
  LICENSE.APACHE. Pinned to gfx-rs/wgpu 14328f49918cce19f7cc8bf703435968c8293035
  (2026-10-14, naga 30.0.0); snapshot/testdata/rust/MANIFEST.json lists every
  file with its checksum. Known differences from the reference outputs are
  recorded in snapshot/rust_deviations_test.go.

Reference GLSL compiler (cross-check for the GLSL frontend)
  glslangValidator: KhronosGroup/glslang tag vulkan-sdk-1.4.341.0, commit
  f0bd0257c308b9a26562c1a30c4748a0219cc951 (reports 11:16.2.0, the build the
  Vulkan SDK 1.4.341.1 ships). CI builds this pinned tag
  (.github/scripts/install-glslang.sh) and compiles the GLSL corpus and matrix
  rows with it, so our acceptances and refusals are checked against the
  reference compiler at one version. Recorded 2026-11-16.

Current scope
  Frontends: WGSL; SPIR-V input (phases 1-3 of the design, ported from Rust
  naga's front/spv: types, constants, decorations, globals, control flow, calls,
  images and sampling, atomics, subgroups, the combined image sampler split, the
  entry-point wrapper, row-major matrix members with their reads and stores (a
  whole-array store and a matrix that is not square stay refused), and the
  Coherent/Volatile memory decorations; nagac -from-spirv turns a binary into
  SPIR-V, MSL, HLSL or GLSL); GLSL input — preview: Vulkan GLSL 440/450/460 and
  the GL 3.30 core / ES 3.00 dialects, with subgroup operations and
  textureQueryLod not implemented yet.
  Backends: SPIR-V, MSL, GLSL, HLSL; DXIL (experimental, not in Rust naga).
  Rust naga's WGSL and DOT outputs are not implemented; Rust naga has no GLSL
  frontend, so ours is our own implementation.

Vendored SPIR-V grammar
  testdata/upstream/github.com/KhronosGroup/SPIRV-Headers/ vendors four files
  of Khronos SPIRV-Headers at tag vulkan-sdk-1.4.341.0 (commit
  04f10f650d514df88b76d25e83db360142c7b174, 2026-01-21), with LICENSE and
  PROVENANCE; internal/spvnames and spirv/internal/spvenums are generated from
  the grammar and a drift test holds them to it.
